{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-smul","title":"lem:submersion-inner-smul","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":774,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:submersion-inner-smul","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-space-smul]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:submersion-inner-smul","line":1220,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The induced form is constant on fibers]\n\\label{lem:submersion-inner-smul}\n\n\\uses{lem:horizontal-space-smul, def:submersion-inner, lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}\n\n\n\n\nUnder the hypotheses of Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-space-smul}, $\\beta_{a\\cdot x}=\\beta_x$ on $T_{\\pi(x)}M$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:horizontal-space-smul,def:submersion-inner,lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}\n\\sketch With $\\Phi=d(a\\cdot {-})_x$, the map $\\Phi L_x$ is a horizontal right inverse of $d\\pi_{a\\cdot x}$, hence equals $L_{a\\cdot x}$ by Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}. Metric invariance then gives $\\beta_{a\\cdot x}(u,v)=\\beta_x(u,v)$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The induced form is constant on fibers] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7375626d657273696f6e2d696e6e65722d736d756c\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-space-smul\">↗ lem:horizontal-space-smul</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asubmersion-inner\">↗ def:submersion-inner</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec</a> <p></p>Under the hypotheses of Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-space-smul\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-space-smul\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d73706163652d736d756c\">3</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\beta _{a\\cdot x}=\\beta _x$\">$\\beta _{a\\cdot x}=\\beta _x$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_{\\pi (x)}M$\">$T_{\\pi (x)}M$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-space-smul\">↗ lem:horizontal-space-smul</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asubmersion-inner\">↗ def:submersion-inner</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec</a> \\sketch With <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi =d(a\\cdot {-})_x$\">$\\Phi =d(a\\cdot {-})_x$</span>, the map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi L_x$\">$\\Phi L_x$</span> is a horizontal right inverse of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi _{a\\cdot x}$\">$d\\pi _{a\\cdot x}$</span>, hence equals <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_{a\\cdot x}$\">$L_{a\\cdot x}$</span> by Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d6c6966742d6c696e6561722d73706563\">7</a>. Metric invariance then gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\beta _{a\\cdot x}(u,v)=\\beta _x(u,v)$\">$\\beta _{a\\cdot x}(u,v)=\\beta _x(u,v)$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-space-smul","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-congr","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-space-smul","title":"lem:horizontal-space-smul","label":"lem:horizontal-space-smul"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner","title":"def:submersion-inner","label":"def:submersion-inner"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","label":"lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-congr","title":"lem:submersion-inner-congr","label":"lem:submersion-inner-congr"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:submersion-inner-smul","title":"lem:submersion-inner-smul","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[The induced form is constant on fibers]\n\\label{lem:submersion-inner-smul}\n\n\\uses{lem:horizontal-space-smul, def:submersion-inner, lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}\n\n\n\n\nUnder the hypotheses of Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-space-smul}, $\\beta_{a\\cdot x}=\\beta_x$ on $T_{\\pi(x)}M$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:horizontal-space-smul,def:submersion-inner,lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}\n\\sketch With $\\Phi=d(a\\cdot {-})_x$, the map $\\Phi L_x$ is a horizontal right inverse of $d\\pi_{a\\cdot x}$, hence equals $L_{a\\cdot x}$ by Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}. Metric invariance then gives $\\beta_{a\\cdot x}(u,v)=\\beta_x(u,v)$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-space-smul","title":"lem:horizontal-space-smul","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion-inner","title":"def:submersion-inner","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}